From: "George V. Neville-Neil" <gnn@FreeBSD.org>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 06:46:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sched_ule: Add cache-miss-aware priority adjustment using
 hwpmc

Extend the ULE scheduler to read LLC-miss hardware performance counters
and penalize cache-hostile threads by up to 50 priority levels. One
hostile child per CPU is pinned via cpuset; a single friendly child
floats freely. The feature is off by default, controlled by four sysctl
knobs under kern.sched.ule.cachemiss_*, and compiles in only with
HWPMC_HOOKS.

New files: sys/kern/sched_pmc.[ch] (per-CPU PMC lifecycle),
tests/sys/kern/sched_cachemiss/ (24 ATF test cases),
tools/regression/sched_cachemiss/ (benchmark).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
